            <ArticleTitle>Can a &quot;Smart Form&quot; increase physicians' satisfactions with managing patient health behavior risks? Results of a physician satisfaction survey.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1047</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Results of a pilot study suggest that the Coronary Artery Disease and Diabetes Mellitus Smart Form may help clinicians in managing diet and exercise in patients with chronic diseases by making patient handouts and exercise prescriptions readily available at the time of the visit.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
